OL,3,GNEWSAWater firm pleads guilty after
OL,4,Afour killed in blast
OL,5,
OL,6,FA water company has pleaded guilty to
OL,7,Fhealth and safety charges after an
OL,8,Fexplosion at one of its sites killed
OL,9,Ffour workers, including a teenage
OL,10,Fapprentice.
OL,12,FLuke Wheaton, 16, Ray White, 57, Brian
OL,13,FVickery, 63, and Mike James, 64, died
OL,14,Fin the blast at Wessex Water's
OL,15,Ftreatment site in Avonmouth, Bristol,
OL,16,Fin December 2020.
OL,18,FA police investigation into
OL,19,Fmanslaughter was dropped in 2024 but
OL,20,Fthe Health and Safety Executive (HSE)
OL,21,Fbrought its own charges earlier this
OL,22,Fyear.
OL,23,APub: 13-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
